    description: "Rename the dependency-link field on tracker items from `before` to `isbefore` so its directionality is self-documenting. Under the CLI canonical semantic, `X.before = [Y]` means 'X runs before Y' (X blocks Y). The field name `before` is ambiguous — readers can flip it in their head to 'Y must come before X', which is exactly what caused the TUI inversion bug fixed in PR #2981 (WI-tubot/WI-botol confusion). A name like `isbefore` reads unambiguously: `X.isbefore = [Y]` → 'X is before Y' → X first.\\n\\n**Scope (rough):**\\n- Data model: rename field in CompiledItem, add_fields/remove_fields plumbing, store serialization/deserialization.\\n- Ops file compatibility: decide whether old ops files (which reference 'before') need migration, a read-time alias, or a one-shot rewrite. The tracker has ~years of accumulated ops with 'before:' entries across .agent/tracker and .agent/tracker-workspace.\\n- CLI: update --before/--add-before/--remove-before/--add-blocked-by/--remove-blocked-by flag names or keep flags and only rename the internal field.\\n- TUI: update field label rendering (already correct directionally post-PR-2981).\\n- Web/serve: update REST/WS payload field names.\\n- Validation: schema rules referencing 'before'.\\n- Tests: widespread fixture + assertion updates.\\n- AGENTS.md + trackerize playbook: update any lingering references.\\n\\n**Open questions for human review:**\\n1. Is the clarity benefit worth the cross-cutting migration cost? The 2-line TUI label fix (PR #2981) already resolves the immediate confusion.\\n2. If yes: breaking change (rename + refuse old) or compatibility (read both, write new)? The tracker is append-only ops-backed, so old ops files cannot be rewritten without invalidating hashes — probably read-both-write-new is the only viable path.\\n3. Do we also rename the CLI flag `--before` to `--isbefore`? Consistency argues yes; muscle-memory argues for keeping the flag as an alias.\\n4. Scope vs. reward: should this be deferred indefinitely unless another directional bug surfaces, or prioritized because it prevents future confusion?\\n\\nContext: conversation 2026-04-11, user jgstern observed after PR #2981 'yikes. maybe if we changed before to isbefore?' Do not work on this item until a human triages it."  # c252
    fields: {}  # c252
